{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 139, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a missing input-to-output residual helps much more than swapping an existing conv or pool on edge 3 for skip."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the edge-3 shortcut, cutting edge 5 removes a main path into the output node and can nearly disconnect the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 5 is already absent, removing edge 4 leaves node 3 fed only by edge 3, which removes most of the learned computation."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node 1 does not feed the output directly, removing its input edge loses less, so the harm is smaller."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 2 is none, edge 1 is node 2's only input, so cutting it makes the edge-5 path dead."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 1 is none, edge 2 is node 2's only input, so removing it disconnects node 2 and the edge-5 path."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping the valuable residual skip for a conv hurts, while replacing none or avg_pool with conv tends to help."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a connection where there was none restores information flow, whereas replacing a conv3x3 with skip loses capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where the edge was missing gives a big